</div>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Among these documents, the insurance certificate should explicitly state a <em>100% declared‑value marine transit insurance</em>.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This means the insurer agrees to cover the full market value of the bike, providing maximum protection against any loss or damage during maritime or inland transit.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>It also simplifies claim settlement, as the insurer will not deduct depreciation or other adjustments.</span></li></ul>

<p>In practice, you should obtain the following steps before shipment:</p>

<ul>
<li>Verify that the RC and PUC are up‑to‑date and free of any pending fines.</li>
<li>Request a self‑attested copy of the RC and a certified PUC from the local transport office.</li>
<li>Contact your insurer to confirm coverage and obtain a written confirmation of the 100% declared value.</li>
<li>Engage a reputable carrier who can issue an IBA‑approved bilty and provide a tracking ID for real‑time monitoring.</li>
</ul>

<p>By ensuring each of these documents is accurate, self‑attested, and up‑to‑date, you mitigate legal risks, avoid delays at checkpoints, and guarantee that your bike is fully protected throughout its journey from Salempur to its destination.</p></div>
